expected_issues.description:
`preload` branch calls `immichAsset(url);` without awaiting/handling rejection. If it throws before entering the `try/finally` (e.g., `caches.open` failure), it will create an unhandled rejection. Consider `void immichAsset(url).catch(() => {/* swallow/log */});` to make intent explicit and avoid noisy logs.

```suggestion
  } else if (event.data.type === 'preload') {
    const urlstring = event.data.url;
    const url = new URL(urlstring, event.origin);
    void immichAsset(url).catch(() => {
      // optional: log to console for debugging
    });
  }
};
```

